menu "Kernel Configuration"

config HOMECORE_KERNEL_MAIN_STACK_SIZE
    int "Kernel stack size"
    default 3072
    range 256 8192
    help
        Bytes reserved at the top of RAM for the main stack, shared by the
        shell, BASIC, and interrupt handlers. File commands peak at about
        0.9 KB. BASIC needs about 910 bytes plus up to 230 bytes per nesting
        level, bounded by HOMECORE_SHELL_BASIC_MAX_NESTING: about 2.75 KB at
        the default of 8. The mem command reports the high-water mark.
        Overflow is not detected and corrupts the heap.

config HOMECORE_KERNEL_STDIO_BUFFERED
    bool "Buffer standard input and output"
    default y
    help
        Let newlib allocate its default buffers for stdin and stdout on first
        use, about 1 KB each from the heap. Disable on small-RAM boards to make
        both streams unbuffered; each character then passes directly to the
        console device.

endmenu
